### <2> Making a request at the office

**Lesson objective:** to understand the content of a request made to strangers or at public institutions.

#### Vocabulary
- 실례하다 - excuse me
- 저기 - excuse me
- 음 - um
- 어 - uh
- 자 - okay
- 아 - ah
- 저 - well
- 체크 카드 - debit card
- 신분증 - identification card
- 글쎄요 - well, let me see
- 연장하다 - to extend or prolong
- 출입국 관리 사무소 - Immigration Office
- 서류 - document
- 재학 증명서 - certificate of student registration
- 뵙다 - to meet (used when meeting people above you)
- 퇴근하다 - to leave one's office or get off from work
- 신청 - registration
- 지나가다 - to go past
- 음성 안내기 - voice guide

#### Let's listen

1. **Polite Requests**
   - (1) 저, 실례합니다만 이 선생님 좀 바꿔 주시겠어요?
     *Um, excuse me but may I speak to the teacher?*

   - (2) 미안합니다만 그날 다른 약속이 있어서요.
     *I'm sorry but I have another appointment on that day.*

   - (3) 저기, 죄송합니다만 관리비를 어떻게 내는지 좀 알려 주시겠어요?
     *Excuse me but can you tell me how I should pay for the maintenance fees?*

   - (4) 감사합니다만 다음 역에서 내립니다.
     *Thank you but I'm getting off at the next station.*

#### Extended Dialogues

**3~4. Letao and Office Worker**
리타오: 저, 실례합니다만 비자를 연장하려고 하는데 출입국관리사무소가 어디에 있는지 아세요?
*Letao: Um, excuse me. I'm trying to extend my visa but do you know where the immigration office is?*

사무실 직원: 지하철 5호선 오목교역에서 내려서 한 20분쯤 걸어가면 됩니다. 지도를 보고 찾아가세요. 인터넷으로 예약하면 금방 끝나니까 미리 예약 하세요. 필요한 서류는 모두 준비하셨습니까?
*Office worker: You get off at Omokgyo Station from the Subway Line 5 and walk about 20 minutes. Find your way by looking at the map. You can be done quickly if you make your appointment through the internet. Have you prepared all the necessary documents?*

리타오: 아, 재학 증명서가 없는데 한 장 부탁드립니다. 제 이름은 리타오입니다.
*Letao: Oh, I don't have my certificate of student registration so may I have one, please? My name is Letao.*

사무실 직원: 네, 잠시만 기다리세요.
*Office worker: Yes, please wait a minute.*

**5~7. Nora and Office Worker**
노라: 저기, 최 과장님을 뵈러 왔는데 자리가 어디인지 아세요? 어제 과장님과 전화한 학생입니다. 아르바이트 때문에 오늘 만날 약속을 했습니다.
*Nora: Excuse me. I've come to see Mr. Choi, the head of the department. Do you know where his desk is? I'm the student who spoke to him on the phone yesterday. We made an appointment today because of a part-time job.*

사무실 직원: 최 과장님은 오늘 다른 회사에서 회의가 있어서 나가셨는데 거기에서 바로 퇴근하실 거예요.
*Office worker: Mr. Choi had a meeting with another company today so he left the office. He will be getting off work directly from that place.*

노라: 아, 제가 너무 늦게 왔군요. 그럼 죄송합니다만 이 아르바이트 신청 서류 좀 과장님께 전해 주실 수 있으세요? 제가 내일은 수업 때문에 다시 올 수 없을 것 같아서요.
*Nora: Oh, I see that I've come too late. I'm sorry, but could you please give this part-time job application to Mr. Choi for me? I don't think I can come again because I have class tomorrow.*

사무실 직원: 네, 서류는 저한테 주십시오. 여기에 성함과 전화번호를 남겨 주시겠어요?
*Office worker: Yes, you can give me your application. Can you leave your name and phone number over here?*

노라: 여기 있습니다. 좀 부탁드리겠습니다.
*Nora: Here it is. I'll just ask you for this favor.*

#### Let's read

I returned from visiting the National Museum of Korea for the first time since I came to Korea. I got off at Ichon Station of the Subway Line 4 but didn't know where to exit so I asked a man passing by for directions.

"Um, excuse me. I'm trying to go to the National Museum but do you know which exit I must take to get there?"

The man kindly taught me where to go so I was able to easily find it. I went into the National Museum for free without paying any money. I wanted to listen carefully to the explanations while touring the museum so I went to borrow a foreign language voice guide.

"Excuse me, but I'd like to borrow an English voice guide. What should I do?"

"You can borrow one if you hand in your ID card and 3,000 won."

I slowly walked around the museum while listening to the explanations through the voice guide so it was easy to understand and really fun. Yuki is really interested in Korean history so I think I'll go again with her. The next time I visit the museum, I want to sign up for a tour guide so I can listen to the explanations in person and tour the museum.

