It was my first time going to a Korean hospital, so I was a bit scared and worried. There were many patients waiting to see the doctor at the hospital. While I was waiting, I thought about how I would explain my symptoms in Korean.

It was my turn, so I went in to see the doctor. The doctor kindly asked me where I was in pain and when it started and then waited for me to answer. After hearing what I said, he gave me a few tests and then told me that I had a serious cold.

He said it was probably because I slept with the air conditioner on every night. He said that I mustn't eat cold foods because my throat is swollen. The doctor told me to keep my throat warm and to take medicine for three days. Then he told me that because my cold will become more serious if I continue to sleep with the air conditioner on, I must not leave it on at night until my cold is better.

