**Q:** Hello? I am a foreign student studying Korean in Korea. I'm not that good in Korean so is there any hobby that can help me learn Korean? It would be great if it was free since I am an overseas student.

**A:** Hello. I've been in Korea for five years. Let me tell you the things I frequently did when I first came to Korea. These are hobbies that you can easily do and have fun doing even if you don't speak Korean well.

**1. Penpals with a Korean friend**
Penpalling used to be done by writing letters or through email but these days having a penpal is made easier and more convenient through a mobile application or SNS. You can make friends and learn more about the Korean language or culture if you have a penpal.

**2. Beautiful letter writing**
Writing beautiful letters by hand can also be a good hobby. Writing is about making a design, so it is fine even if you don't know Korean that well. You only need paper and a pen to do this and since you will be writing a lot of Korean, it is helpful to your Korean studies.

**3. Writing a blog**
Do you know how to make your own blog? If so, then create a blog in Korean. If you write about your life in Korea on your blog like a diary, it will be a tremendous help to your Korean studies. If you also upload pictures on your blog, you can remember all the food you enjoyed and the places you visited often after you have returned to your hometown.

