## Korean Culture Sections

### Korean Culture: Popular Locations for Meeting Appointments
Where are the popular places for making an appointment to meet people in Seoul? The five most popular places searched on the internet to make appointments to meet people are Hongdae, Gangnam station, Apgujeong, Garosugil, and Itaewon. Among these places, Hongdae is number one and many young people go there because of the good restaurants, cafes with a nice atmosphere, stylish clothes stores, fun clubs and bars, and various street performances like busking. You get a more elegant atmosphere in places like Gangnam station, Apgujeong, and Garosugil. Itaewon is the place you can experience the various cultures of different countries.

### Korean Culture: Using the Library
- **National Library of Korea:** As the largest library in Korea, there is an abundance of materials. The facilities of the digital library are especially nice.
- **Namsan Public Library:** This is the oldest library in Korea that opened its doors in 1922. It is located in Namsan, which has beautiful scenery. The library holds exhibitions, lectures, and culture classes.
- **Seoul Metropolitan Library:** This library was placed inside the old city hall building and offers the service of being able to search the data of all the libraries in the city of Seoul.

### Korean Culture: Automatic Bill Payment Machine
If you go to a bank, you can see the Automatic Bill Payment Machine next to the Automatic Teller Machine. In the past, you would have to go to the window, take a number ticket, and then wait a long time in order to pay your housing management fees, gas bill, water bill, or phone bill. But now, with the Automatic Bill Payment Machine, you can make your payments without waiting in lines as long as you have your bankbook or card. Recently, you can even make your payments with greater ease with your credit card or online banking.

### Korean Culture: Medicine you can buy at the convenience store
Are you only able to buy medicine at the pharmacy? These days, you can also buy medicine at the convenience store. When it's late at night or a weekend when the pharmacy is closed, you can find all kinds of medicine you need at the convenience store such as painkillers, digestion medicine, pain relief patches, fever medicine, and cold medicine. However, if you take too much medicine, a problem can arise, so you must not buy several of the same medicine at one time. Try using the convenience store to get your medicine when you urgently need it.

### Korean Culture: Korea's Blockbuster Movies
In Korea, if a movie had an audience of over 10 million people, it is considered to have been a great show. Until 2017, there were a total of 15 movies that exceeded an audience of 10 million people. Among these successful shows, the movies with historical background made up the most number, namely 명량 (ROARING CURRENTS, 2014), 암살 (Assassination, 2015), 태극기 휘날리며(TaeGukGi: Brotherhood Of War, 2003). There were also many other movies about love between family members (7번 방의 선물 (Miracle in Cell No.7, 2012) and 해운대 (Haeundae, 2009)) and societal issues (베테랑 (Veteran, 2015) and 택시 운전사(A Taxi Driver, 2017).

### Korean Culture: Life Index
A life index is a number that expresses the extent of influence the weather has on our lifestyle. If we look at the life index together with the weather forecast, our lives will be more convenient. There are indexes for discomfort level, ultraviolet rays, food poisoning, and even car washing. For example, the discomfort index tells us how a person's mood can go up or down depending on the temperature and humidity. In a summer with high temperatures and much humidity, the discomfort index is high, so people become very irritated.